 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "# 05 \u2014 Same abstract graph, certified distinct spatial embeddings\n\nThis benchmark asks:\n\n\\[\n\\text{same abstract graph}\n\\;+\\;\n\\text{independently certified inequivalent embeddings}\n\\;\\Longrightarrow\\;\n\\text{how many are distinguished by the Yamada polynomial?}\n\\]\n\nLevel 1 fixes a single trivalent theta graph with\n\n\\[\nV=2,\\qquad E=3,\\qquad (\\deg u,\\deg v)=(3,3),\n\\]\n\nand changes only the embedding by tying local knots into one edge.\n\n**No Yamada value is used to construct, select, or certify the examples.**\nCertification uses the ordinary-knot HOMFLY-PT invariant of the three constituent\ncycles, computed independently with Topoly. Different constituent-cycle HOMFLY\nmultisets imply inequivalent spatial theta graphs. Equality would not prove\nequivalence, so only pairwise-distinct signatures are admitted.\n\nTopoly 1.1.0 accepts nested coordinate lists as structures and deterministic\n`Closure.CLOSED` calculations; it is already pinned in the repository benchmark\ndependency group.\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "from __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport itertools\nimport re\nimport sys\n\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport networkx as nx\nimport numpy as np\nimport sympy as sp\n\nROOT = Path.cwd().resolve()\nwhile ROOT != ROOT.parent and not (ROOT / \"pyproject.toml\").exists():\n    ROOT = ROOT.parent\nif not (ROOT / \"src\" / \"knotted_graph\").exists():\n    raise RuntimeError(\"Run this notebook from inside the KnottedGraph checkout.\")\n\nSRC = ROOT / \"src\"\nsys.path.insert(0, str(SRC))\n\nimport knotted_graph\nfrom knotted_graph.projection import compute_yamada_polynomial\n\ntry:\n    import topoly\n    from topoly import homfly\n    from topoly.params import Closure\nexcept ImportError as exc:\n    raise ImportError(\n        \"Install the benchmark environment first: \"\n        \"uv sync --all-extras --group benchmark\"\n    ) from exc\n\nkg_path = Path(knotted_graph.__file__).resolve()\nif SRC not in kg_path.parents:\n    raise RuntimeError(f\"A stale knotted_graph was imported from {kg_path}\")\n\nprint(\"KnottedGraph:\", kg_path)\nprint(\"Topoly:\", Path(topoly.__file__).resolve())\n\nA = sp.Symbol(\"A\")\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 1. Fixed abstract theta graph\n\nThe three parallel edges are labelled only to define the controlled construction.\nEvery generated sample retains the same two vertices and three edges; only the\n`pts` array of `e1` changes.\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "U = np.array([-1.10, 0.0, 0.0])\nV = np.array([ 1.10, 0.0, 0.0])\n\ndef base_theta(n=600):\n    t = np.linspace(0.0, 1.0, n)\n    x = U[0] + (V[0] - U[0]) * t\n\n    e1 = np.c_[x, np.zeros_like(t), np.zeros_like(t)]\n    e2 = np.c_[x,  0.88*np.sin(np.pi*t),  0.10*np.sin(2*np.pi*t)]\n    e3 = np.c_[x, -0.88*np.sin(np.pi*t), -0.10*np.sin(2*np.pi*t)]\n\n    G = nx.MultiGraph()\n    G.add_node(\"u\", pos=U.copy())\n    G.add_node(\"v\", pos=V.copy())\n    G.add_edge(\"u\", \"v\", role=\"e1\", pts=e1)\n    G.add_edge(\"u\", \"v\", role=\"e2\", pts=e2)\n    G.add_edge(\"u\", \"v\", role=\"e3\", pts=e3)\n    return G\n\nG0 = base_theta()\nassert G0.number_of_nodes() == 2\nassert G0.number_of_edges() == 3\nassert sorted(dict(G0.degree()).values()) == [3, 3]\nprint(\"base theta:\", G0.number_of_nodes(), \"vertices,\", G0.number_of_edges(), \"edges\")\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 2. Independently verified prime-knot templates\n\nWe use deterministic polygonal parametrizations for four prime knots:\n\\(3_1,4_1,5_1,7_1\\). The *labels* are convenient names, but the certificate\nbelow is the raw HOMFLY-PT fingerprint returned by Topoly with translation\ndisabled.\n\nUsing the raw invariant avoids any dependence on Topoly's knot-name dictionary:\nif two HOMFLY fingerprints differ, the knots are definitely inequivalent.\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "def normalize_template(P):\n    P = np.asarray(P, dtype=float)\n    P = P - P.mean(axis=0)\n    scale = np.max(np.linalg.norm(P, axis=1))\n    if scale <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"degenerate knot template\")\n    return P / scale\n\ndef torus_template(p, q, n=1800):\n    t = np.linspace(0.0, 2*np.pi, n, endpoint=False)\n    r = 1.0 + 0.38*np.cos(q*t)\n    P = np.c_[r*np.cos(p*t), r*np.sin(p*t), 0.38*np.sin(q*t)]\n    return normalize_template(P)\n\ndef figure8_template(n=2000):\n    t = np.linspace(0.0, 2*np.pi, n, endpoint=False)\n    P = np.c_[\n        (2.0 + np.cos(2*t))*np.cos(3*t),\n        (2.0 + np.cos(2*t))*np.sin(3*t),\n        np.sin(4*t),\n    ]\n    return normalize_template(P)\n\nPRIME_TEMPLATES = {\n    \"3_1\": torus_template(2, 3),\n    \"4_1\": figure8_template(),\n    \"5_1\": torus_template(2, 5),\n    \"7_1\": torus_template(2, 7),\n}\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "### Topoly HOMFLY fingerprint\n\nFor a deterministic closed polygon, `Closure.CLOSED` returns one deterministic\nresult. `translate=False` requests the invariant itself rather than a dictionary\nlookup. The normalized string is used only as a stable equality key inside this\nnotebook.\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "def _stable_fingerprint(value):\n    return re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \"\", str(value))\n\ndef homfly_fingerprint(points):\n    P = np.asarray(points, dtype=float)\n    if len(P) < 4:\n        raise ValueError(\"a closed polygon needs at least four samples\")\n    if np.allclose(P[0], P[-1]):\n        P = P[:-1]\n\n    value = homfly(\n        P.tolist(),\n        closure=Closure.CLOSED,\n        tries=1,\n        translate=False,\n        poly_reduce=True,\n        chiral=False,\n        minimal=False,\n        hide_trivial=False,\n        max_cross=25,\n        cuda=False,\n        run_parallel=False,\n    )\n    return _stable_fingerprint(value)\n\ndef translated_knot_name(points):\n    P = np.asarray(points, dtype=float)\n    if np.allclose(P[0], P[-1]):\n        P = P[:-1]\n    value = homfly(\n        P.tolist(),\n        closure=Closure.CLOSED,\n        tries=1,\n        translate=True,\n        poly_reduce=True,\n        chiral=False,\n        minimal=True,\n        hide_trivial=False,\n        max_cross=25,\n        cuda=False,\n        run_parallel=False,\n    )\n    return str(value)\n\nt = np.linspace(0.0, 2*np.pi, 900, endpoint=False)\nUNKNOT_CURVE = np.c_[np.cos(t), np.sin(t), np.zeros_like(t)]\nUNKNOT_FP = homfly_fingerprint(UNKNOT_CURVE)\n\nPRIME_FP = {}\nfor name, P in PRIME_TEMPLATES.items():\n    fp = homfly_fingerprint(P)\n    PRIME_FP[name] = fp\n    print(f\"{name:4s}: translated={translated_knot_name(P)!r}\")\n    if fp == UNKNOT_FP:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"{name} template was classified as HOMFLY-trivial\")\n\nif len(set(PRIME_FP.values())) != len(PRIME_FP):\n    raise RuntimeError(\"Prime templates are not pairwise separated by HOMFLY.\")\n\nprint(\"PASS: four nontrivial prime templates have pairwise-distinct HOMFLY fingerprints.\")\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 3. Turn each closed knot into a certified local-knot arc\n\nA short polygonal segment is removed from each closed knot. Closing the remaining\nlong arc by the straight chord between its endpoints must reproduce the same\nHOMFLY fingerprint as the original closed template.\n\nThe search also favors cuts whose complementary arc stays reasonably compact\nrelative to its endpoint chord; this makes the later insertion geometrically safe.\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "def basis_from_chord(a, b):\n    x = np.asarray(b-a, dtype=float)\n    L = np.linalg.norm(x)\n    if L < 1e-10:\n        raise ValueError(\"cut endpoints are too close\")\n    ex = x/L\n\n    ref = np.array([0.0, 0.0, 1.0])\n    if abs(ex @ ref) > 0.90:\n        ref = np.array([0.0, 1.0, 0.0])\n\n    ey = np.cross(ref, ex)\n    ey /= np.linalg.norm(ey)\n    ez = np.cross(ex, ey)\n    return np.vstack([ex, ey, ez])\n\ndef complementary_arc(P, start, gap):\n    n = len(P)\n    end = (start + gap) % n\n    if start < end:\n        return np.vstack([P[end:], P[:start+1]])\n    return np.asarray(P[end:start+1], dtype=float)\n\ndef arc_shape_metrics(arc):\n    a, b = arc[0], arc[-1]\n    B = basis_from_chord(a, b)\n    Q = (arc - 0.5*(a+b)) @ B.T\n    chord = np.linalg.norm(b-a)\n\n    x_half = 0.5*chord\n    longitudinal_ratio = np.max(np.abs(Q[:,0])) / x_half\n    transverse_ratio = np.max(np.linalg.norm(Q[:,1:], axis=1)) / chord\n    return longitudinal_ratio, transverse_ratio\n\ndef certified_open_template(name, P):\n    target_fp = PRIME_FP[name]\n    candidates = []\n    n = len(P)\n\n    for gap_fraction in (0.025, 0.04, 0.06, 0.085, 0.12, 0.16, 0.22):\n        gap = max(4, int(round(gap_fraction*)))\n        for start in np.linspace(0, n-1, 32, dtype=int):\n            arc = complementary_arc(P, int(start), gap)\n            if len(arc) < 20:\n                continue\n            try:\n                long_ratio, trans_ratio = arc_shape_metrics(arc)\n            except ValueError:\n                continue\n\n            # Prefer a compact long-knot representation.\n            score = long_ratio + 0.35*trans_ratio\n            candidates.append((score, long_ratio, trans_ratio, arc))\n\n    candidates.sort(key=lambda row: row[0])\n\n    for score, long_ratio, trans_ratio, arc in candidates[:80]:\n        if long_ratio > 2.0:\n            continue\n        if homfly_fingerprint(arc) == target_fp:\n            print(\n                f\"{name}: certified open arc \"\n                f\"(longitudinal={long_ratio:.2f}, transverse={trans_ratio:.2f})\"\n            )\n            return arc\n\n    raise RuntimeError(\n        f\"Could not find a compact straight-closure-certified open arc for {name}.\"\n    )\n\nOPEN_TEMPLATES = {\n    name: certified_open_template(name, P)\n    for name, P in PRIME_TEMPLATES.items()\n}\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 4. Insert local knots into one theta edge\n\nA positive linear map sends each certified open arc into a protected slot on\n`e1`. Positive longitudinal and transverse scale factors preserve the local-knot\ntype. The two untouched theta edges remain far outside the slot interiors.\n\nFive single-knot cases plus four two-slot connected-sum constructions give ten\ncandidate embeddings including the trivial theta.\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "def map_open_arc(arc, left, right, transverse_radius):\n    left = np.asarray(left, dtype=float)\n    right = np.asarray(right, dtype=float)\n    midpoint = 0.5*(left+right)\n\n    target = right-left\n    target_len = np.linalg.norm(target)\n    if target_len <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"invalid target slot\")\n\n    a, b = arc[0], arc[-1]\n    B0 = basis_from_chord(a, b)\n    Q = (arc - 0.5*(a+b)) @ B0.T\n\n    source_len = np.linalg.norm(b-a)\n    Q[:,0] *= target_len/source_len\n\n    tr = np.max(np.linalg.norm(Q[:,1:], axis=1))\n    if tr <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"degenerate transverse template\")\n    Q[:,1:] *= transverse_radius/tr\n\n    ex = target/target_len\n    ref = np.array([0.0,0.0,1.0])\n    if abs(ex@ref) > 0.90:\n        ref = np.array([0.0,1.0,0.0])\n    ey = np.cross(ref,ex)\n    ey /= np.linalg.norm(ey)\n    ez = np.cross(ex,ey)\n    Bt = np.vstack([ex,ey,ez])\n\n    mapped = Q @ Bt + midpoint\n    mapped[0] = left\n    mapped[-1] = right\n    return mapped\n\ndef line(a, b, n=80, endpoint=False):\n    return np.linspace(np.asarray(a,float), np.asarray(b,float), n, endpoint=endpoint)\n\ndef knotted_e1(prime_factors):\n    if len(prime_factors) == 0:\n        return np.linspace(U, V, 700)\n\n    if len(prime_factors) == 1:\n        slots = [(-0.47, 0.47, 0.25)]\n    elif len(prime_factors) == 2:\n        slots = [\n            (-0.82, -0.08, 0.15),\n            ( 0.08,  0.82, 0.15),\n        ]\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(\"controlled suite uses at most two local-knot factors\")\n\n    pieces = []\n    cursor = U.copy()\n\n    for factor, (xa, xb, radius) in zip(prime_factors, slots):\n        left = np.array([xa,0.0,0.0])\n        right = np.array([xb,0.0,0.0])\n\n        pieces.append(line(cursor, left, 70, endpoint=False))\n        mapped = map_open_arc(\n            OPEN_TEMPLATES[factor],\n            left,\n            right,\n            transverse_radius=radius,\n        )\n\n        # Numerical safety check: local knot remains concentrated near its slot.\n        if np.max(np.linalg.norm(mapped[:,1:], axis=1)) > radius*1.001:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"mapped local knot escaped its transverse slot\")\n        if mapped[:,0].min() < xa-0.38 or mapped[:,0].max() > xb+0.38:\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                f\"{factor} local-knot arc has excessive longitudinal overshoot\"\n            )\n\n        pieces.append(mapped[:-1])\n        cursor = right\n\n    pieces.append(line(cursor, V, 90, endpoint=True))\n    P = np.vstack(pieces)\n    P[0] = U\n    P[-1] = V\n    return P\nd—P–ÄL@≈9QR